    <h2>Mission</h2>
    <p>
      Silver Lining of Hope, Inc provides free investigative research and
      advocacy for families of missing persons, unsolved and hidden homicides,
      and unidentified persons, and for survivors of domestic violence. We act
      as a partner resource for law enforcement, detectives, and prosecutors —
      compiling records, cleaning data, and surfacing connections that help
      move cases forward.
    </p>

    <h2>Vision</h2>
    <p>
      A future where no case goes cold for lack of attention, no family is
      left to investigate alone, and every missing and unidentified person in
      our region is accounted for in one public, searchable record.
    </p>

    <h2>Our commitments</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Our services are free to families and law enforcement — always.</li>
      <li>We treat every victim, every family, and every case with dignity. We are not a true-crime entertainment outlet.</li>
      <li>We work alongside law enforcement, not around it.</li>
      <li>We protect the privacy and safety of the people we serve, especially survivors of domestic violence.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      Silver Lining of Hope, Inc is a 501(c)(3) public charity, EIN 39-2169099,
      based in Indiana and serving families across Indiana, Ohio, Illinois,
      Michigan, and Kentucky.
    </p>
